hape faster but maybe reduce potential for high fan patterns (like Seven Pairs, which requires no exposed melds).  \n\nGiven I have exposed melds already, Seven Pairs impossible. All Pungs possible if I get two more pungs. That\u2019s 6 fan. Plus Dragon Pung 2 fan = 8 fan \u2014 enough. So maybe aim for All Pungs: need two more pungs.  \n\nSo maybe I should not Chi, but try to get pungs. That means keep T5 pair, try to get another T5. Keep B3, try to get another B3, etc. Chi would break possible pung chances (B2, B3 would be used in chow).  \n\nThus **Pass** might be better to try to draw into pung possibilities.  \n\n**Answer:** Pass"}
